"answer": "Project Zenith is a strategic initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, with a later description defining it as an AI-driven framework for predictive analytics in aerospace. The project was initiated in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader and a kickoff meeting on July 15th. Key developments include the approval of a $2M budget, an adjustment to $550,000 for specific scope realization, and a $55,000 allocation for compliance. The team expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing. A strategic partnership with TechInnovate was secured to aid in AI research. The project reached a significant milestone with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was sought by the end of November."
